+// Zocial World Stage 2 ("Ironwood") pool policy (ADR-018 § 1 Stage 2 amendment, § 3), MIT OR
+// Apache-2.0 like the rest of WebZjs. Replaces the Stage-1 Sapling-beta policy (`sapling_beta.rs`).
+//
+// * receive:  the account's full unified address (Orchard-family receiver — where Ironwood payments
+//             arrive since NU6.3 — + Sapling + transparent), a shielded-only unified address
+//             (Orchard-family + Sapling) for player payments, and the plain Sapling (zs1) and
+//             transparent (t1) encodings of the same receivers;
+// * spend:    Ironwood, Sapling and legacy Orchard notes (the Orchard pool is withdraw-only since
+//             NU6.3); transparent funds are only ever spent by `shield` (and, inside a TEX
+//             withdrawal, the ephemeral output of its own first transaction);
+// * pay:      a unified address with an Orchard-family receiver → Ironwood (version-6 transaction);
+//             otherwise its Sapling receiver; a Sapling address → Sapling; a transparent address →
+//             only for withdrawal outputs; a TEX address (ZIP 320) → only for withdrawal outputs,
+//             through the upstream ephemeral-address two-step flow; a unified address's transparent
+//             receiver is never paid;
+// * change:   always Ironwood (`change::IronwoodChangeStrategy`), also when Sapling or Orchard notes
+//             are spent; shielding sends the shielded value to Ironwood;
+// * upgrade guard: unchanged from Stage 1 — before any transaction is proposed, proved or (legacy
+//             path) broadcast, lightwalletd's consensus branch must be one this build supports and
+//             the one this build's rules give the tip, and no upgrade may activate within the expiry
+//             window.
+//
+// Everything is enforced twice: the proposal is constrained by zcash_client_backend's own knobs
+// (spend policy, change strategy, proposed version, single-receiver recipient addresses), and the
+// result is re-checked (`check_proposal` before proving, `check_transaction` before broadcasting).
+
